  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>etravirine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>J05AG04</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, oral dosing <small>(PK_1C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Green B et al. 2017</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>adult subjects with HIV</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>etravirine</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_etravirine/Etravirine_Green2017_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>apparent total clearance (CL/F)</td><td>41.7</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>apparent central volume of distribution (V c/F)</td><td>972</td><td>L</td><td><small>V/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>first-order absorption rate constant (k a)</td><td>1.16</td><td>h</td><td><small>t1/2ka </small></td></tr><tr><td>absorption lag-time</td><td>1.32</td><td>h</td><td><small>tlag</small></td></tr><tr><td>between-subject variability on relative bioavailability (F)</td><td>35.5</td><td></td><td><small>IIV</small></td></tr><tr><td>KA</td><td>0.455</td><td>h−1</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr></table><h4>About etravirine</h4><p>Etravirine is a non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor used to treat HIV infection. It is an approved antiviral, authorised in the European Union for HIV infections.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q414762\">Wikidata Q414762</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Etravirine\">Etravirine</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Green B et al. (